    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$2.03 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e. Pork shoulder is the best protein value in the meat case, and a long slow roast is what turns it from a cheap cut into a great one.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePork shoulder is the cheapest good protein in the store.\u003c/strong\u003e Look for it labeled Boston butt or picnic shoulder. Bone-in usually costs less per pound and the bone adds flavor while it roasts.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy garlic by the head.\u003c/strong\u003e This rub uses real garlic, mashed with oregano and salt, and jarred minced garlic will not give you the same punch for the money.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eMarinate overnight and the seasoning cost drops.\u003c/strong\u003e Given 12 to 24 hours, a small amount of garlic, vinegar, lime and dried oregano flavors the entire roast. Rushed, you would need three times as much.",
